.\" PAM module manual for Howdy Next
.TH PAM_HOWDY 8 "July 16, 2026" "Howdy Next 3.3.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pam_howdy \- PAM facial authentication module for Howdy Next
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pam_howdy.so
[\fBworkaround=\fR\fIoff|input|native|native-input\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pam_howdy.so
authenticates a PAM user with Howdy Next facial recognition.
.PP
The module reads Howdy configuration from
.I /etc/howdy/config.ini
and user face models from
.IR /etc/howdy/models/ .
These paths are expected to remain root-controlled and non-user-writable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fBworkaround=\fR\fIoff|input|native|native-input\fR
Set the password prompt workaround for this PAM service. The default is
\fBoff\fR.
.RS
.TP
\fBoff\fR
Do not start or stop a concurrent password prompt.
.TP
\fBnative\fR
Use PAM conversation control to stop Howdy's concurrent password prompt after
successful face authentication. This mode does not fall back to input injection.
.TP
\fBnative-input\fR
Try native prompt handling first, then fall back to the input workaround when a
usable TTY is unavailable or native prompt handling cannot be installed.
.TP
\fBinput\fR
Use a
.I /dev/uinput
Enter key workaround to stop the concurrent password prompt. The injected key
is not addressed to the PAM conversation and may be received by another
application that currently has keyboard focus. This mode is less preferred than
.B native
and may be less reliable on some lock screens.
.RE
.PP
This option is intentionally service-local. It is configured on the
.B pam_howdy.so
line and is not read from
.IR config.ini .
.SH SETUP
.SS Basic
For a PAM consumer where Howdy should run as a sufficient authentication method:
.PP
.nf
auth  sufficient  pam_howdy.so
.fi
.SS TTY, Login, And Sudo
For TTY-backed services that call PAM before collecting a password, put Howdy
before
.BR pam_unix (8).
Use
.B workaround=native
if Howdy should run concurrently with the password prompt and stop that prompt
after successful face authentication:
.PP
.nf
auth  optional     pam_exec.so /usr/bin/linux-enable-ir-emitter run --config /etc/linux-enable-ir-emitter.toml
auth  sufficient   pam_howdy.so workaround=native
auth  sufficient   pam_unix.so try_first_pass nullok
auth  sufficient   pam_fprintd.so
.fi
.SS Graphical Authorization Prompts
Graphical PAM consumers, including graphical Polkit prompts, may not provide a
usable TTY. If Howdy must stop a concurrent password prompt, use
.B workaround=native-input
to prefer native prompt handling where available and fall back to input
injection otherwise:
.PP
.nf
auth  sufficient   pam_howdy.so workaround=native-input
.fi
.PP
The input fallback sends Enter through
.IR /dev/uinput .
It is not targeted to the PAM prompt and may instead reach another application
that currently has keyboard focus. Validate this behavior for each graphical
consumer before enabling it.
.SS Lock Screens That Collect Input Before PAM
Some lock screens, including
.BR waylock ,
collect password input before calling PAM. For those services, validate the
already-submitted password first, then fall through to Howdy and fingerprint
authentication:
.PP
.nf
auth  optional     pam_exec.so /usr/bin/linux-enable-ir-emitter run --config /etc/linux-enable-ir-emitter.toml
auth  sufficient   pam_unix.so try_first_pass nullok
auth  sufficient   pam_howdy.so workaround=off
auth  sufficient   pam_fprintd.so
.fi
.PP
When a PAM authentication token already exists,
.B pam_howdy.so
does not start the native or input workaround, even if a workaround option is
configured.
.SH SECURITY NOTES
Do not make
.I /etc/howdy
or
.I /etc/howdy/config.ini
world-readable to support unprivileged lock screens. Howdy Next expects the
protected source config and model paths to remain root-controlled.
.PP
PAM consumers that run authentication as the regular user use the installed
.B howdy-auth-helper
setuid helper to prepare temporary root-controlled runtime copies of the
protected config and enrolled model before recognition.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/howdy/config.ini
Main Howdy configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/howdy/models/
User face models directory.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/howdy/howdy-auth-helper
Setuid helper used for unprivileged PAM consumers. The exact path depends on
the installation prefix and library directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR howdy (1),
.BR pam (8),
.BR pam_unix (8),
.BR pam_fprintd (8)
